                <pb facs="0190" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1949v05/pg176"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>At his press and radio news conference of November 30, Secretary of State Acheson
                    issued a statement which took note of the United Nations General Assembly
                    resolution of November 18 regarding the Greek case and the suggested embargo of
                    arms shipments to Bulgaria and Albania. In his statement, the Secretary of State
                    announced that the United States would abide faithfully by the recommendation,
                    would continue its policy of refusing to permit the export of such materials to
                    Albania and Bulgaria, and would take all possible steps itself and in
                    cooperation with other countries to suppress clandestine traffic to Albania and
                    Bulgaria. For the text of the statement, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, December 12, 1949, page 911.</p>
            </div>
